  "notes": "United Electronics Company (eXtra, ticker 4003) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/434_0_2026-02-18...). Auditor PwC. Board of Directors authorised the statements for issue on 12 February 2026 (used as filed_at). The five primary statements (printed pages 7-12) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.5x); the notes (printed page 13 onward) are digital text. Amounts are in thousands of Saudi Riyals (scale 1000). eXtra runs a consumer Islamic-financing (BNPL/instalment) book alongside electronics retail: revenue combines 'Sales and services' (6,675,993k), 'Income from Islamic financing contracts' (769,012k) and 'Income from payroll advances' (1,110k); the financing receivables sit in 'Investment in Islamic financing contracts' (mapped as long_term_investments / short_term_investments for the non-current / current portions). income_taxes_and_zakat is Zakat expense + Income tax expense combined (also carried split). operating_income is a computed subtotal (gross profit less S&D, G&A, net impairment losses on financial assets and other expenses, plus other income). impairment_charges is 'Net impairment losses on financial assets' (mostly on the financing book). long_term_debt / current_debt are the non-current / current 'Borrowings'; IFRS 16 lease liabilities are mapped separately. contract_liabilities is the non-current 'Deferred revenue' (extended-warranty / service contracts); defined_benefit_obligation is 'Employee benefit obligations'. depreciation_amortization sums depreciation of property and equipment, depreciation of right-of-use assets and amortisation of intangible assets from the cash-flow statement. capex is 'Payments for purchases of property and equipment'. interest_paid is 'Finance cost paid'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat and income tax paid'. The cash-flow statement reconciles with no separate foreign-exchange effect line. Statement page references are the printed page numbers: profit or loss and OCI 7, financial position 8, changes in equity 10, cash flows 11.",
